[t=022 agent] Aiden Mercer has shown great enthusiasm for reading this quarter, especially with 'Holes,' which he finished quickly. His connection between the story and his own journaling shows thoughtful engagement, and he is motivated to try writing his own story this summer. Ava Patel has demonstrated resilience and courage in her writing, sharing personal experiences with sensitivity. Despite challenges, she is making progress and expressing herself more openly through her essays. Brianna Okafor enjoys family traditions and brings warmth to her writing, especially when describing her time cooking with her grandmother. Her ability to connect language and culture enriches her work. Carlos Reyes-Vega: 6E-104 Carlos Reyes-Vega Two write-ups in February for verbal conflict during lunch — restorative-justice circle held; situation resolved. when my brother got deported, my mom stopped sleeping. I am the one who walks my little sister to school now. I am only twelve but I feel like I am thirty some days. Books are the only place I get to be a kid again. Daniela Cruz exhibits patience and dedication in her work, drawing parallels between cooking and writing that show her thoughtful approach to learning. Ethan Williams is adapting well to new challenges and finds joy in science experiments, which engage him regardless of distractions. His perseverance is commendable. Fatima Hassan has a strong appreciation for poetry and is eager to explore writing in her native language, showing a deep connection to her cultural identity. Grace Lindgren has made significant progress in expressing her feelings through journaling, developing from simple entries to more complex writing, including poetry. Hiro Tanaka enjoys shared reading experiences with his family, which bring joy and laughter, enriching his connection to literature. Imani Brooks has embraced technology to support her writing, finding new ways to express her thoughts that feel authentic and comfortable. Jamal Foster is working hard to manage his emotions and behavior, using physical activity as a positive outlet. His honesty and effort are important steps forward. Kalea Wong has shown remarkable strength and maturity in supporting her family during a difficult time, which has deeply influenced her personal growth and writing. Liam O'Sullivan: 6E-113 Liam O'Sullivan 504 — ADHD, extended time on assessments Repeated tardies — three parent meetings. I know I am late a lot. The mornings are hard at my house because my little brother has autism and getting him out the door takes everything we have. I am not making excuses, just explaining. Maya Goldberg is making steady progress in speech and communication, gaining confidence and clarity in her expression. Noah Bennett is taking important steps toward positive change, engaging in family therapy and reflecting on his choices with a desire to improve. Olivia Nguyen is an avid reader and creative writer, producing an impressive volume of work and developing her storytelling skills. Priya Sharma finds bravery in caring deeply about characters and stories, showing emotional growth through her reading and writing. Ryan Kim balances academics and athletics well, applying discipline learned on the basketball court to his classroom efforts. Sofia Martinez is adjusting to a new environment with determination, using writing as a tool to express herself and build confidence. Tyler Johnson: 6E-120 Tyler Johnson Three tardies in March — parent conference scheduled. My stepdad works nights so mornings are loud and rushed. I am not trying to be late, I swear. I like this class because Ms. Reyes lets us write about real stuff instead of made-up prompts. Uma Desai enjoys creative expression through poetry and values the time spent cooking with her family, which inspires her writing. Victor Chen takes his time to communicate clearly in writing, showing patience and care in his work. Willa Anderson has shown resilience through a difficult experience with her horse and channels her emotions into powerful writing. Xavier Thompson: 6E-124 Xavier Thompson Phone confiscated twice in February for filming in hallway. I make short videos for fun — not during class, I know the rules. This quarter I tried writing a script instead of filming and it was harder than I expected. Turns out dialogue is weird on paper. Yara Ali demonstrates thoughtfulness and openness in sharing her experiences with fasting, helping peers understand her culture. Zach Morrison benefits from accommodations that support his testing experience and is learning to value careful work over speed. Amira Khalil navigates complex family dynamics with sensitivity and expresses herself in multiple languages, enriching her writing. Brandon Lee: 6E-128 Brandon Lee Detention in January for disrupting class — agreed to check in with counselor biweekly. I act out when I am confused because asking for help feels like admitting defeat. This essay was about the first time I raised my hand and the answer was wrong and nobody laughed. That mattered more than being right. Chloe Davis volunteers in her community and writes with heartfelt emotion, connecting deeply with her subjects. Dante Romano finds ways to cope with social challenges by creating routines that work for him, reflecting thoughtful problem-solving. Elena Vasquez: 6E-131 Elena Vasquez My grandma watches me after school while my mom works doubles at the diner. She tells stories about crossing the border that I am only old enough now to understand. This essay is for her, even though she cannot read English. Finn Murphy: 6E-132 Finn Murphy We lost our apartment in October and stayed with my aunt for two months. I did not tell anyone at school until Ms. Reyes asked how I was doing and actually waited for an answer. Having one adult who knows helps. Gia Washington adapts presentations to manage anxiety, demonstrating self-advocacy and growth. Holden Price connects patience learned in woodworking to writing, finding new appreciation for both skills. Isla Fernandez shares her love of music and its emotional power, using songwriting as a way to support her family. Jasper Cole uses assistive technology to express his ideas honestly, focusing on authenticity over perfection in his writing.
